---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Skill Foundry"
  description="Learn what information Skill Foundry receives, how it is used, and the choices available when you use the website."
  canonical="https://hub.skillfoundry-web.workers.dev/privacy/"
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-container">
        <p class="legal-eyebrow">PRIVACY</p>
        <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-lead">This policy explains what information Skill Foundry receives when you use the website, how it is handled, and the choices available to you.</p>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-body">
      <div class="legal-container">
        <div class="legal-content">
          <section class="legal-section-block">
            <h2>1. Information we receive</h2>
            <p>Skill Foundry is a public learning and resource website. You do not need to create an account, register, or provide payment details to browse its public pages and resources.</p>
            <p>If you submit a message through a contact form, the form asks for your name, email address, subject and message. Please do not include passwords, payment information or other sensitive personal details in a message. Contact information is used to understand and respond to the enquiry and is not published on the website.</p>
            <p>When a page is requested, the website's hosting and security infrastructure may process technical information such as an IP address, browser and device details, requested URL and request time. This information may be used to deliver the site, prevent abuse, troubleshoot errors and maintain security.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-section-block">
            <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
            <p>Information submitted through the contact form is intended to help us reply to questions, feedback, collaboration enquiries or reports about the website and its resources. Technical request information may be used to operate, protect and improve the website.</p>
            <p>Skill Foundry does not publish contact-form submissions or use them to create public user profiles. We do not sell personal information.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-section-block">
            <h2>3. Cookies and local storage</h2>
            <p>The website saves your selected light or dark theme in your browser's local storage using the key <code>sf_theme</code>. This lets the site remember your display preference when you return. It is browser storage, not an advertising cookie.</p>
            <p>Skill Foundry does not currently intentionally set advertising cookies or use its own analytics to build profiles for personalised advertising. Hosting, security or third-party services may process technical information as part of delivering their services. Browser settings let you clear local storage, although doing so may reset your saved theme preference.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-section-block">
            <h2>4. Hosting, email services and external links</h2>
            <p>Skill Foundry uses Cloudflare's website and Worker infrastructure to serve the site and handle website requests. That infrastructure may process technical request information as described above, subject to the provider's own terms and privacy practices.</p>
            <p>The contact form is designed to send submitted messages to Skill Foundry by email through Resend when the email-delivery configuration is enabled. If delivery is enabled, the information in the message is processed by that service to deliver the email. If the required configuration is unavailable, the form reports that the message cannot currently be delivered; it should not be treated as successfully submitted.</p>
            <p>Pages may also link to external websites, software, AI tools and social platforms. When you follow an external link, that provider's privacy policy and practices apply to your activity there. Skill Foundry does not control those services.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-section-block">
            <h2>5. Data retention and your choices</h2>
            <p>Skill Foundry does not currently publish a fixed retention period for contact enquiries. If a message is successfully delivered by email, it may remain in the receiving email account and related service records according to the settings and retention practices of those services. We aim to keep information only for as long as it is reasonably needed to handle the enquiry, maintain records or meet applicable obligations.</p>
            <p>You can choose not to submit the contact form and can clear the saved theme preference through your browser's site-data settings. If you want to ask about, correct or request deletion of information you have sent, use the Contact us button in the final section. We will consider the request and explain if any information must be retained for a legitimate or legal reason.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="legal-section-block legal-section-last">
            <h2>6. Policy updates and contact</h2>
            <p>This policy may be revised when the website's features or data practices change. The version published on this page is the current version. For a privacy-related question or request, contact Skill Foundry using the button below.</p>
            <a class="legal-contact-button" href="/contact/?subject=Question%20about%20this%20Privacy%20Policy">Contact us</a>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    min-height: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-container {
    width: min(780px, calc(100% - 48px));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .legal-hero {
    padding: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px) 0 22px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line, #1E293B);
    background: transparent;
  }

  .legal-title {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    color: #F8FAFC;
    font-size: clamp(27px, 4vw, 34px);
    font-weight: 750;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .legal-updated { margin: 10px 0 0; color: #64748B; font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.4; }

  .legal-contact-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: fit-content; margin-top: 18px; min-height: 40px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid #A8C8DF; border-radius: 9px; background: #C5DDED; color: #183247; font-family: inherit; font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 750; text-align: center; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; }

  .legal-lead {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 680px;
    color: #94A3B8;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal-body {
    padding: 24px 0 0;
  }

  .legal-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  :global(main .legal-page .legal-content) { gap: 0 !important; }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block) {
    padding: 0 0 22px;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block + .legal-section-block) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sf-page-divider);
    padding-top: 22px;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block h2) {
    margin: 0 0 18px !important;
    color: var(--sf-page-heading);
    font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 20px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block p) {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 0 14px !important;
    color: var(--sf-page-copy);
    font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.68;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block p:last-of-type) {
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-last) {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block a) {
    color: var(--sf-page-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block code) {
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sf-page-border);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--sf-page-surface);
    color: var(--sf-page-heading);
    font-size: .92em;
  }

  :global(main:has(.legal-page) > .sf-global-cta) {
    padding-top: 36px !important;
  }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .legal-updated,
  :global(html.light-theme) .legal-updated { color: #64748B; }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .legal-title,
  :global(html.light-theme) .legal-title {
    color: #0F172A;
  }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .legal-lead,
  :global(html.light-theme) .legal-lead {
    color: #475569;
  }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .legal-section-block h2,
  :global(html.light-theme) .legal-section-block h2 {
    color: #0F172A;
  }

  :global([data-theme="light"]) .legal-section-block p,
  :global(html.light-theme) .legal-section-block p {
    color: #334155;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-container {
      width: calc(100% - 32px);
    }

    .legal-hero {
      padding: 26px 0 20px;
    }

    .legal-title {
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .legal-body {
      padding-top: 20px;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block) {
      padding-bottom: 20px;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block + .legal-section-block) {
      padding-top: 20px;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block h2) {
      margin-bottom: 16px !important;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block p) {
      margin-bottom: 12px !important;
      font-size: 14.5px;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-block p:last-of-type) {
      margin-bottom: 0 !important;
    }

    :global(.legal-page .legal-section-last) {
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    :global(main:has(.legal-page) > .sf-global-cta) {
      padding-top: 24px !important;
    }
  }
</style>
